          <b>{{ r.title }}</b>
          <span>{{ r.detail }}</span>
        </span>
        {%- if r.project %}<button class="r-go" data-id="{{ r.project }}">OPEN</button>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <div class="toolkit">
      <span>PYTHON</span><span>OSMNX</span><span>PYROSM</span><span>NETWORKX</span><span>GEOPANDAS</span><span>QGIS</span><span>SPACE SYNTAX</span><span>PCA / K-MEANS</span><span>CNN</span><span>JETSON ORIN</span><span>GRASSHOPPER</span><span>REVIT / PYREVIT</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="about">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="about">
      <div>
        <div class="band-head" style="margin-bottom:var(--s5)"><h2>About</h2></div>
        <p>I trained as an architect and stopped drawing buildings when I realised the questions I cared about were about the space between them. Now I work as a spatial data scientist, mostly on cities, mostly with street networks, sensors and whatever the city will let me measure.</p>
        <p>Bengaluru is where I live and the place most of this work tests itself against. London is where the thesis was done. Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata and Chennai appear because a comparison is only fair if every city is cut the same way.</p>
        <p>My pattern, for better and worse, is saying yes to something before I fully understand it and then refusing to put it down until I do. That is how a person who had never touched a breadboard ended up building a sensor.</p>
        <div class="contact">
          <a class="btn" href="mailto:prakritisrimal@gmail.com">Email</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/psrimal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/prakriti-srimal-7390ab1a5/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div class="fact"><dt>ROLE</dt><dd>Senior Urban Data Scientist, Urban Intelligence Lab, Bengaluru</dd></div>
        <div class="fact"><dt>EDUCATION</dt><dd>MArch Urban Design, UCL Bartlett B-Pro, RC14 Machine Thinking Urbanism, 2023. Architecture, BMS College of Engineering</dd></div>
        <div class="fact"><dt>2026</dt><dd>Nominated for the Sidara Endeavour Program for Scenario Simulator</dd></div>
        <div class="fact"><dt>AWARDS</dt><dd>SEED Chairman Award for Sounds of the City. Gold medal, World Architecture Student Awards 2022. Student Award, Media Architecture Biennale 2023</dd></div>
        <div class="fact"><dt>PUBLISHED IN</dt><dd>ArchDaily, Arch Hive, ArchiDiaries, Inspireli, UCL Bartlett</dd></div>
        <div class="fact"><dt>BASED</dt><dd>Bengaluru, India</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

